Parley is part of the KDE Education Project, it's a flashcard program built
specifically to showcase different styles of foreign-language learning. Its
free and only built for linux as far as I'm aware.

CSV (a .csv file) is literally just a text file with "comma separated
values." Excel and OpenOffice can export and import as .csv, and it's really
easy to transfer a plain text file (such as a list of gismu!) into csv
format for quick creation and manipulation of "decks" of flashcards.

